      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "We present three cases of central post-stroke pain after right hemorrhagic or ischemic stroke associated with severe impairment of cutaneous sensibility but preservation of stimulus-evoked pain from periosteum. This is the first such report of dissociation of cutaneous- from deep-tissue sensibility loss."},
